<title>RUSSIA: Russia to sell 2.14 percent of Slavneft Dec 27.</title>
<headline>Russia to sell 2.14 percent of Slavneft Dec 27.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia will sell 2.54 million shares or 2.14 percent of the capital of AO NK Slavneft with bids accepted from November 27 to December 27 at a minimum price of 5,000 roubles a share, the Federal Securities Corporation (FFK) said on Friday.</p>
<p>Results of the cash auction will be published by January 29, 1997. Shares in Slavneft are not actively traded.</p>
<p>Slavneft, a Russian-Belarussian joint venture, is one of a dozen vertically integrated Russian oil groups created over the last few years. Its main operating unit is Megionneftegaz.</p>
<p>-- Moscow newsroom, (7095) 941 8520</p>
